# Gitignore-style patterns for things that must not be published as static assets.
#
# `.wrangler/` is wrangler's own local state -- the miniflare cache, the local
# Durable Object SQLite files, and its temp bundles. It appears inside the repo
# root, which is also `assets.directory`, so without this it would be uploaded
# with the game.
#
# Deliberately minimal. Publishing the rest of the tree is an intentional decision
# recorded in wrangler.jsonc, and trimming it is a separate change with its own
# reasoning -- not something to slip in alongside a multiplayer feature.
#
# NOTE what this does NOT fix, because the first version of this file claimed it
# did: `wrangler dev` watches `assets.directory` for changes, and this file does
# not exclude anything from that watcher. With the directory set to the repo root,
# wrangler's own writes into `.wrangler/tmp` retrigger it, and the server reloads
# several times a second while answering nothing. That is why local multiplayer
# development uses wrangler.dev.jsonc, which has no assets block at all.
# The remote Cloudflare checkout includes Git's packed history. It is not part of
# the game and a pack can exceed Workers' 25 MiB per-asset limit.
.git
.wrangler
